{ "name": "Dread Cuts",
  "id": "dread_cuts",
  "feel": "The cut the film was built with. Hard cuts on the words, a low camera looking up at them, a tilted horizon that drifts, and a slow push or a small orbit on every shot, so the place feels wrong without the camera ever showing off.",
  "recipe": "A hard cut on a line start or an action, every 1.2-3.5 s, never two near-identical angles in a row. Lens fov 26-32, camera at chest-to-head height. Every shot moves: a push of 10-15 % or an orbit of 10-15 deg. Roll 2-5 deg, changing side from shot to shot. Dead still only for the silence. The last shot pushes in on the character who knows.",
